@startuml btrie-trie-node-layout
' ============================================================================
' btrie-trie-node-layout.puml — the B-trie trie node (512 bytes = 128 × 4-byte ptrs).
' Source: docs/theory/disk-tries/02-b-trie.md (Askitis & Zobel 2009), § Page Layout.
' Drawn as a CONTIGUOUS colored byte table (offset column + field column) hosted in
' a floating note; rows share borders (no gaps). The 124 middle pointers are elided
' in one grey row; the pointer encoding is preserved as a text block below the table.
' Full-cell color via Creole |<#hex>| cells.
' Color key:  blue #BBDEFB  child pointers (one per ASCII char)
'             grey #ECEFF1  elision of the 124 middle pointers
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam TitleFontSize 15
skinparam noteFontSize 14
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #37474F
}

title B-trie trie node — 512 bytes = 128 × 4-byte pointers

note as TN
|= bytes |= field |
|<#BBDEFB> 0..3 |<#BBDEFB> Pointer[0] — child for char 0 (NUL) |
|<#BBDEFB> 4..7 |<#BBDEFB> Pointer[1] — child for char 1 |
|<#ECEFF1> ⋮ |<#ECEFF1> Pointer[2 .. 126]  (124 more) |
|<#BBDEFB> 508..511 |<#BBDEFB> Pointer[127] — child for char 127 (DEL) |

**Pointer encoding** (4 bytes each):
MSB = 0 → bucket (block number) · MSB = 1 → trie node (block number, MSB set)
all zeros → null pointer.  16 trie nodes fit in one 8 KB block.
end note

legend bottom
| Color | Field |
|<#BBDEFB>| child pointer (one per ASCII char) |
|<#ECEFF1>| elision of the 124 middle pointers |
endlegend
@enduml
